{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"f844 TOOK FIVE PLAN REVIEWS. The pattern is the useful artifact, so recording it.\n\n  review 1: BLOCK x4 -- self-contradicting AC (docs/env-vars.md 'no diff' while adding nine env\n            vars), REBAR_LLM_CONFIG_FILE described in PRESENT TENSE though it is sibling cb6f's\n            unbuilt deliverable, and the fallback sub-object schema never defined at all.\n  review 2: BLOCK x2 -- the parser was ORPHANED. My own fix for review 1 narrowed Scope to keep\n            llm/config.py under the 800 cap (it sits at 777), which left nothing extracting the\n            model_classes sub-table and handing it to parse_class_slots. A parser nothing calls.\n  review 3: BLOCK x1 -- the Approach claimed precedence 'CLI -c llm.KEY > env > file > default'\n            but the code never read cli_overrides_for('llm'), so rebar -c llm.frontier.model=gpt-4o\n            was SILENTLY IGNORED. A false claim in the plan, not a missing detail.\n  review 4: PASS, signed.\n\nTWO OF THE THREE LATER BLOCKS WERE CAUSED BY MY OWN REMEDIATIONS. That is the lesson: a material\nplan edit invalidates the prior PASS in SUBSTANCE, not just in bookkeeping. The close gate said so\nmechanically ('stale-material: the plan was materially edited since review') and it was right to.\n\nTHREE DISTINCT STALENESS MODES seen this run, same remedy, different triggers:\n  stale-head      -- landing a commit moves HEAD and invalidates every outstanding attestation\n  stale-pin-drift -- editing a CHILD invalidates the PARENT's review (it pins dependency material)\n  stale-material  -- editing the ticket's OWN plan invalidates its review\nOnly 'review-plan <id> --status --ref HEAD' (read-only, no LLM) surfaces these cheaply. Check before\nassuming a ticket is claimable/closable; do not spend ~14 min on a speculative re-review.\n\nGERRIT CONFIRMED THE SAME THING INDEPENDENTLY. Pushing the amended patchset printed:\n  'The following approvals got outdated and were removed: LLM-Review+1, Verified+1'\nSo the +1/+1 I had been reading on 1102 covered the PRE-remediation patchset. Reading a vote without\nchecking which patchset it belongs to is how a stale green gets trusted -- the same failure as the\n1048 TRIVIAL_REBASE vote-copy earlier in this epic.\n\nWHAT THE BEHAVIOURAL ORACLE COULD NOT CATCH, worth carrying to every remaining ticket: 16/16 held-out\ntests passed and six mutations were caught, and the change would STILL have failed CI on doc drift,\nbecause docs/env-vars.md is generated by a scanner that only sees LITERAL env-var strings and the\nfirst implementation built the nine names with an f-string. Module size and derived-file\nregeneration live OUTSIDE the test net. They belong in the implementer brief; I briefed the first\nand missed the second.\n\nSTATE: f844 local commit 0a1645847 pushed to 1102, both gates re-running. Suite 8182 passed / 74\nskipped / 0 failed. a574's code fix (typed LLMConfigError naming REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION, plus the\ntwo guard tests that stop 'always raise' from passing) is implemented and mutation-checked but\ndeliberately UNCOMMITTED and separate from f844's commit."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785491844759075001,"uuid":"ba796c0b-e973-4caf-bf30-16693a9852bc"}